From 2ce5152f3965328616f27e1f14661a6ec750176e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Jul 2026 08:56:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06867/11362] [outer-loop] ARC re86 round-4: L6->L7, executes
 round-3's decoded assignment

Round-4 codex gpt-5.6-sol attempt on re86 solved L7 by directly executing
round-3's "route to the known assignment" recommendation: a deformed
color-11 small plus, a 19x7 color-9 rectangle, and an independently-offset
color-8 large plus advanced levels_completed to 7. No new color-mapping
discovery was needed -- round 3 had already decoded the assignment; this
session just executed cleanly, avoiding round 3's early-assignment
exploration cost and repaint trap.

Independently re-verified by the outer loop: 5x fresh env.reset() + replay
via a new resolver priority branch, sliced to the first 519 of 698 actions
(the full trace continues into unsuccessful L8 exploration past the win),
all 5 confirmed level=7, state=GameState.NOT_FINISHED.

L8 adds two color-1 resize fixtures and a paint-swatch barrier; a resized
rectangle still gets repainted from an adjacent swatch through a visually
clear corridor, showing paint contact is stricter than rendered-cell
overlap. No L8 win.

reproducible_total_levels 148 -> 149. arc_count_integrity_lint.py exit 0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
